From 4e4d98a7a253f2cf90de7cafc219d0b29bfe79af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philip Mueller <claude@philipmueller.ch>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 06:45:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 43/43] feat(harbor_agent): mask context-limit rollouts, detect
 OpenCode overflow

A rollout that the context limit ended (failure class context_overflow:
the prompt no longer fit, or a reply was cut by the context ceiling)
trains with its verifier reward, usually 0, although the policy neither
finished nor failed the task. With Terminus-2 at a 24k context this was
a third to a half of all rollouts in a training step.

New config flag harbor_mask_context_overflow (default false, so the
default behaviour does not change): when set, every context_overflow
rollout sets instance_config.mask_sample, with and without training-token
capture, as harbor_mask_infra does for infra rollouts. The response still
carries failure_class, failure_detail and the failure_<class> fields.

OpenCode overflows were not classified at all and read as ok. OpenCode
writes no agent_error_flags.json, and Gym's vLLM model server answers
vLLM's HTTP 400 "maximum context length" with an empty completion with
finish_reason "length" and no usage (unless
propagate_context_overflow_errors is set). OpenCode ends its loop on any
reply that is not a tool call, also on "length", without an error and
with exit code 0, so the verifier runs and the rollout looks normal.

When a trial has no flags file, harbor_agent now derives the same fields
from OpenCode's `run --format=json` log (agent/opencode.txt, downloaded
with the agent logs): context_overflow when
- the last step finished with "length" and no tokens at all, after steps
  that all reported tokens (OpenCode requests stream usage, so every
  answered call reports prompt tokens): the model server's placeholder,
  the prompt did not fit;
- OpenCode reported a ContextOverflowError, or an error whose message is
  a context-length error (the 400 propagated);
- the last reply hit "length" within max(256, 1 %) tokens of
  harbor_agent_kwargs.model_info.max_input_tokens, the rule Terminus-2
  uses for a reply cut by the context ceiling.
A "length" reply with room left stays ok. The detail says which case
applied. The event shapes follow OpenCode 1.17.11 (cli/cmd/run.ts,
session/processor.ts); Terminus-2's path is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Philip Mueller <claude@philipmueller.ch>
